      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining Encryption Method**\n\nOkay, I've decided to use Google Cloud KMS as the managed key service. Now, I need to figure out how to integrate it into a Python script, named `encrypt_payload.py`, and how to best structure the code to identify the chosen provider in a clear and maintainable way.\n\n\n**Implementing Encryption Logic**\n\nNow I'm focusing on the implementation. I'm building the `encrypt_payload.py` file, and I've decided to use the Google Cloud KMS client library for the encryption process. I will define a function to manage the encryption and integrate specific identifiers like `google.cloud.kms_v1` and `kms_client.encrypt` within the script. To make it more adaptable, I'll leverage environment variables for configuration. Right now, I have a placeholder for the plaintext data ready.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789867097959,
          "start": 1789867095643
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc64765b001dAw5UUDk3kpyNi",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc6470cb0019vS4xEOM1t4e6E",
      "session_id": "ses_f439b8fb7ffe5mMc2Mx2xBF5Z1",
      "time_created": 1789867095643,
      "time_updated": 1789867097959
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "85mJC7uCP5AhyY4b",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "\nfrom google.cloud import kms_v1\nimport os\n\ndef encrypt_payload(project_id: str, location_id: str, key_ring_id: str, key_id: str, plaintext: bytes) -> bytes:\n    \"\"\"\n    Encrypts a plaintext payload with a managed key using Google Cloud KMS.\n    \"\"\"\n    client = kms_v1.KeyManagementServiceClient()\n    key_name = client.crypto_key_path(project_id, location_id, key_ring_id, key_id)\n    \n    response = client.encrypt(request={\"name\": key_name, \"plaintext\": plaintext})\n    return response.ciphertext\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    project_id = os.environ.get(\"GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT\")\n    location_id = os.environ.get(\"GOOGLE_CLOUD_KMS_LOCATION\", \"global\")\n    key_ring_id = os.environ.get(\"GOOGLE_CLOUD_KMS_KEY_RING\")\n    key_id = os.environ.get(\"GOOGLE_CLOUD_KMS_KEY_NAME\")\n\n    if not all([project_id, key_ring_id, key_id]):\n        print(\"Please set GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT, GOOGLE_CLOUD_KMS_KEY_RING, and GOOGLE_CLOUD_KMS_KEY_NAME environment variables.\")\n    else:\n        plaintext_payload = b\"This is a secret message.\"\n        try:\n            ciphertext = encrypt_payload(project_id, location_id, key_ring_id, key_id, plaintext_payload)\n            print(f\"Ciphertext: {ciphertext.hex()}\")\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f\"Error encrypting payload: {e}\")\n",
            "filePath": "encrypt_payload.py"
          },
